# Normalise line endings so the repository's canonical form is always LF.
#
# Without this, an editor or tool reaching into the checkout from Windows
# rewrites whole files to CRLF. Because git had no attribute to normalise
# against and core.autocrlf was unset, those rewrites showed up as a diff
# touching every line with equal insertions and deletions and no content
# change at all — 72 files and ~75k/~75k on one occasion, which then blocked
# the production deploy gate on "working tree has uncommitted changes".
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text files (binaries are left alone) and store
# them LF-normalised in the index; `eol=lf` checks them out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
